---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { PLAN_LIMITS } from '@golem/shared';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Apple"
  description="The terms for using Apple: a beta service, provided as-is, with a free daily quota, your content staying yours, and plain-language rules about acceptable use."
  heading="Terms of Service"
  updated="August 2026"
>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of Apple, the AI building service for Roblox operated by Apple
    Labs. By creating an account or using the service you agree to them. They are short on
    purpose — please actually read them.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>The short version:</strong> Apple is a beta, provided as-is. Your projects are yours.
      Keep your own backups of anything you cannot afford to lose. Don't abuse the service or use
      it to break Roblox's rules. We can change or end the beta, and you can leave — with your
      data — at any time.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. The service</h2>
  <p>
    Apple lets you describe changes to a Roblox place in natural language and have an AI agent
    apply them inside Roblox Studio via the Apple plugin. The service includes the web app, the
    API, and the Studio plugin. Apple is an independent product — we are
    <strong>not affiliated with or endorsed by Roblox Corporation</strong>, and your use of Roblox
    and Roblox Studio remains governed by Roblox's own terms.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Beta status — provided as-is</h2>
  <p>
    Apple is a <strong>beta service, provided "as-is" and "as available"</strong>, without
    warranties of any kind, express or implied. AI systems make mistakes: Apple may write incorrect
    code, misunderstand a request, or modify your place in a way you did not intend. We built undo
    waypoints and checkpoints precisely because of this — use them, and keep independent backups of
    any place you care about. To the maximum extent permitted by law, Apple is not liable for
    lost data, lost revenue, or any indirect or consequential damages arising from use of the beta.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You need an email address to create an account, and you are responsible for what happens under it.</li>
    <li>One person, one account. Creating multiple accounts to multiply the free quota is a fast way to lose all of them.</li>
    <li>You must be old enough to consent to online services in your country, or have a parent or guardian's permission.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Your content stays yours</h2>
  <p>
    You retain all rights to your projects, scripts, prompts and anything Apple generates for you
    in your project. You grant us only the limited license needed to operate the service — to
    store, process and transmit your content in order to do the things you ask Apple to do.
    <strong>We do not use your private content to train AI models</strong> (see the
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>). To the extent Apple's output is protectable, we assign
    any interest we might have in it to you.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Quotas and fair use</h2>
  <p>
    The free tier includes a fixed daily Credits quota (currently {PLAN_LIMITS.free.creditsPerDay}). Quotas, rate limits and
    queueing exist so that the free tier can exist. We may adjust quota numbers with notice in the
    <a href="/changelog">changelog</a>. Attempting to evade quotas, automate accounts, or resell
    access breaks these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Don't use Apple to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>build content that violates Roblox's Community Standards or Terms of Use;</li>
    <li>generate malware, scams, or experiences designed to harm or deceive players;</li>
    <li>attack, probe or overload the service itself;</li>
    <li>infringe someone else's intellectual property.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may suspend accounts that do. Where practical we will warn first.</p>

  <h2>7. Payments</h2>
  <p>
    Apple v1 collects <strong>no payment</strong>. There are no purchases, no subscriptions and
    therefore no refunds — there is nothing to refund. The Pro plan exists only as a waitlist;
    joining it creates no payment obligation. If paid plans launch, they will come with their own
    clearly published pricing and refund terms before anyone is charged.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes and termination</h2>
  <p>
    We may modify or discontinue features of the beta at any time. If we ever plan to shut the
    service down entirely, we will give account holders reasonable notice and a window to export
    their data. You can stop using Apple and delete your account whenever you like — deletion
    works as described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    If these terms change materially, we will note the change in the
    <a href="/changelog">changelog</a> and email account holders before it takes effect. Continued
    use after the effective date is acceptance.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Governing law &amp; contact</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Israel, and disputes belong to the
    competent courts there. Questions first, though:
    <a href="mailto:apple.labs.app@gmail.com">apple.labs.app@gmail.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
